clusters[].networking.networkSegments[].gateway              Yes         Gateway in CIDR (e.g. 10.30.10.1/24); mapped into supervisor by segment name.\line
clusters[].networking.networkingVmKernelInterfaces           Conditional Required for vSAN-ESA and vSAN-OSA only (not VMFS). At least two entries: vMotion, vSAN (required). Optional third: vSAN Witness. Shallow\line
                                                                         / deeper checks validate the child keys below.\line
clusters[].networking.networkingVmKernelInterfaces[].service Conditional One of: vMotion, vSAN, vSAN Witness (exact strings). vMotion and vSAN are required across the array; vSAN Witness is optional.\line
clusters[].networking.networkingVmKernelInterfaces[].vlanId  Conditional VLAN ID 0-4095; must match a segment used for that traffic class.\line
clusters[].networking.networkingVmKernelInterfaces[].netmask Conditional IPv4 netmask for the VMkernel (e.g. 255.255.255.0).\line
clusters[].networking.networkingVmKernelInterfaces[].ipList  Conditional Array of exactly two unique IPv4 addresses (order aligns with esxHosts order).\line
clusters[].networking.networkingVmKernelInterfaces[].gateway Conditional Optional. Used on the vSAN Witness entry only: IPv4 gateway applied via esxcli after the VMkernel exists.\par}
